/target
/result
/result-*

# Screenshots are outputs, not sources: `dtr --screenshot out.png` run in the
# repo must never end up in a commit. Logo renders and the kittest baselines are
# the deliberate exceptions (both go through LFS).
*.png
!assets/**/*.png
# A kittest baseline is an input: egui_kittest fails with "Missing snapshot"
# when it is not there, so these being untracked meant CI compared against
# nothing. The failure artefacts stay ignored, below.
!crates/dtr/tests/snapshots/*.png
!crates/dtr-widgets/tests/snapshots/*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
**/tests/snapshots/**/*.diff.png
**/tests/snapshots/**/*.new.png
**/tests/snapshots/**/*.old.png

# Profiling output: `dtr --cpu-profile`, `scripts/flamegraph.sh` and `perf
# record` all write next to the working directory, and none of it belongs in a
# commit — the inputs are rerunnable in seconds, the files are hundreds of MB.
perf.data
perf.data.*
*.prof
flame.svg
flamegraph.svg
profile.svg
